 :landlock-source-assessment {:source "/usr/include/linux/landlock.h, filesystem rights and warning section"
                              :observed "Header defines deny-by-default handled filesystem rights; REFER is ABI 2, TRUNCATE ABI 3. Files opened before sandboxing are not restricted; header warns chmod, chown, xattr, utime, ioctl and other families are not generally covered. TCP-only ABI 4 network rights are not a deny-all-network solution. Header existence does not prove running kernel ABI, policy availability or unprivileged applicability."
                              :proposal "At minimum ABI 3 with NNP and every applicable write/create/remove/refer/truncate right handled, allow only owned roots by descriptor-relative rules, no writable inherited descriptors. Supplement with independently reviewed seccomp denials for metadata mutation and kernel escape interfaces, not a claim that seccomp filters paths. Review all non-Landlock write channels, procfs, devices, shared memory, io_uring, mmap, hardlinks, and inherited FDs; deny unneeded mechanisms. No privilege/capability elevation. If complete containment cannot be established, do not execute."
                              :next-probe "Separately approved neutral ABI/version query and deny/allow probe only, no GovOne, go compiler, build or tests. Check ABI >=3, restrict_self with NNP, allow a private regular file and deny outside create/write/truncate/rename/link including symlink paths, inherited descriptors, metadata mutation and escape channels; confirm sentinel bytes and metadata outside root unchanged. Probe each relevant syscall ABI and thread/child inheritance. Unsupported, missing, unverifiable or partial coverage is a stop, never a fallback. This probe needs its own reviewed bounded supervisor and consent/effect gate."}
 :network-and-supervision {:network "Deny socket, socketpair, connect, bind, listen, accept/accept4, send/receive and other relevant network and alternate-ABI paths for all families, including AF_UNIX, inherited descriptors, io_uring and child processes. No DNS, network toolchain, providers, models, listeners or ambient proxy. Seccomp arch-check and reject x32/unsupported ABIs. Close inherited FDs except controlled inert stdin and bounded log/control pipes."
                           :attempt-detection "A reviewed trusted seccomp user-notification or equivalent synchronous monitor must record every denied network attempt for every thread/descendant, return EPERM, fail closed if the observer dies, loses notifications or overflows, and independently attest complete event counts. Account for exactly the fixture's one AF_INET socket sanity check per selected test, correlated to its verified site/thread or an equally strong reviewed identity mechanism; any other attempt including one disguised as expected is failure. If exact attribution/coverage cannot be proved, stop rather than assume two total attempts suffice. Probe supervisor death and denial accounting before application execution."
                           :process "Trusted external subreaper/watchdog outside child group; handshake registers PID, starttime and PGID before release. Deny setsid/setpgid/unshare/setns and other escape paths after setup; prohibit uncontrolled detached processes. On any deadline/error, stop launch and perform identity-anchored TERM then KILL with separate bounded deadlines, reap descendants, check group absence and log completion. Never signal a recycled identity. Registration gaps, possible escape, incomplete reap, unknown cleanup or lost monitor => fail closed, retain evidence, no automatic retry or cleanup. Existing typed/Services guards are source primitives, not qualified for this writable Go profile."}
