             :hard-limit-gate "Neither directory permissions, du polling, RLIMIT_FSIZE nor per-file reservation alone enforces aggregate filesystem bytes. No new mount, quota, cgroup or privileged setup is assumed. Admit only if an existing independently reviewed, kernel-enforced bounded writable backing store already available to the user can enforce each total including metadata/links and is separately qualified; otherwise these limits are design budgets only and execution is blocked. No automatic deletion to recover space."
             :memory-cpu "Proposed ceilings: aggregate 4 GiB resident memory and 2 CPU cores, compile wall 1200 s, test wall 180 s, cleanup 15 s TERM plus 15 s KILL/reap, combined log output 16 MiB per stage. GOMAXPROCS=2 and go -p=1 reduce concurrency but do not enforce aggregate CPU/RSS; per-process RLIMIT_AS/CPU likewise cannot enforce a group total. Require existing independently qualified aggregate enforcement or block, not polling-only assurances. Go 1.27.1 and modernc.org/sqlite v1.39.0/libc v1.66.3 are source-grounded reasons to anticipate a heavy cold compile; these ceilings are unmeasured proposals, not expected consumption or a promise of success. A limit failure is a stop, not a retry at a larger limit."
